==French==

===Etymology===
This term originated from the French colonies that became Algeria?Marrocco, where members of the French Foreign Legion suffered extreme boredom in their stockades and took to shooting beetles (''les [[cafards]]'') with their rifles. Le cafard came to mean an extreme depression or sense of pointlessness.

===Verb===
'''[[avoir]] [[le]] [[cafard]]'''

# {{literally}} To have a cockroach.
# {{idiom|lang=fr}} To have the [[blues]]

[[fr:avoir le cafard]]